# Study Hub runs fully locally (browser IndexedDB, nothing locked) when the Supabase values are empty.
#
# To enable sign-in with Google, saved progress and the courses that need an account:
#   1. Set up a Supabase project as described in docs/DEPLOY.md (migrations, providers).
#   2. Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development, and set the same VITE_* values as
#      environment variables on Netlify for the hosted site.
#
# The publishable (anon) key is safe in the browser: row level security restricts every table to
# the signed-in user. Never put the secret / service_role key in any VITE_* variable: those are
# bundled into the app. `npm run check:deploy` refuses to deploy if you do.

# Project Settings -> Data API: https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
# Project Settings -> API Keys: the publishable key (sb_publishable_...) or the legacy anon key.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# Sign-in buttons, in order: Google only by default. "discord", "github" and "email" can be added
# (e.g. google,github); each must also be enabled in Supabase: Authentication -> Sign In / Providers.
VITE_AUTH_PROVIDERS=google

# --- Netlify only (Site configuration -> Environment variables), not needed locally ---
# The edge function reads VITE_SUPABASE_URL above to verify sign-ins against your project's
# public signing keys. Only if your project still signs tokens with the legacy JWT secret
# (Project Settings -> JWT Keys), also set it here, scoped to Functions and marked secret:
# SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=
